<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, reconciliation of independent Tibetan-first and English-first proposals. Four lexical las/karma occurrences and three sems/minds or mind occurrences are separately resolved; opening ablative las is omitted. yod pa ma yin owns the phrase cease to be. sems dang bcas pa is unresolved as a relation here: original ILL:2686 says those who possess a mind, and HGM dang bcas pa permits both possession and accompaniment. Only sems/mind is retained; mind and what comes along with it is not licensed as a whole on that evidence. gsog pa owns collected, not what comes along. sa bcu par is the inflected established work title Sutra of the Ten Levels (HGM 20220); its sa bcu member owns Ten Levels (HGM 20217). The inseparable locative ending stays within the title and receives no separate English alignment. HGM tshor ba po/master and byed pa po/maker cross in English. Great and of all things remain supplied. One med pa is distributed over two no phrases and is omitted. tsam takes the quoted only after word, not the later mind-only quotation. Final mind itself, of things and the explanatory frame are supplied; the last byed pa po/creator and gzhan/other remain lexical atoms, with the distributed negation and bstan frame omitted. No source correction or dictionary promotion is made.</div>
